<body>
    <h1>PRD Unified Multi-Firm Access</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <div class=3D"contentLayout2">
 <div class=3D"columnLayout two-right-sidebar" data-layout=3D"two-right-sid=
ebar">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-moved">DRAFT</sp=
an></p>
   </div>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"cell aside" data-type=3D"aside">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout two-right-sidebar" data-layout=3D"two-right-sid=
ebar">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h1 id=3D"PRDUnifiedMultiFirmAccess-FeaturePositioning">Feature Positio=
ning</h1>
    <h2 id=3D"PRDUnifiedMultiFirmAccess-FeatureOverview">Feature Overview</=
h2>
    <p><span>Unified Multi=E2=80=91Firm Access enables CX to support firm r=
elationships by allowing users to securely operate across multiple firms wi=
thin a single, unified experience across CX, and achieve access parity with=
 NetRep, SecuredZone &amp; R2.</span></p>
    <p>This feature is designed to support two primary multi=E2=80=91firm a=
ccess scenarios:&nbsp;firm <strong>aggregation </strong>and firm<strong> de=
legation.&nbsp;</strong>Unified Multi=E2=80=91Firm Access allows these user=
s to be set up once and granted scoped access to multiple firms, without re=
quiring separate logins or manual firm switching, while ensuring actions ar=
e executed within the correct firm context.</p>
    <p><br></p>
    <h2 id=3D"PRDUnifiedMultiFirmAccess-ProblemStatement">Problem Statement=
</h2>
    <p><span>Multi=E2=80=91firm operating models are well not supported in =
our platforms.&nbsp; While firm relationships such as parent=E2=80=93child =
affiliations or PM sub=E2=80=91advisory agreements may exist in upstream sy=
stems (e.g., Firm360 or operational processes), user access in R2, NetRep a=
nd SecuredZone is configured differently.&nbsp; Users who operate across mu=
ltiple firms must be created, maintained, and authenticated separately for =
each firm, or using inconsistent workarounds, leading to insufficient visib=
ility and control and ultimately creating risk of data leakage and fraud.</=
span></p>
    <p>There are two key relationships that impact a firm's interactions wi=
th NBIN and vice versa:</p>
    <p><strong>Aggregate (Parent) Users</strong></p>
    <p>Firms that operate multiple registered businesses require cross-firm=
 access to supervise and support those businesses.&nbsp; Today this is eith=
er done through issuing of multiple ID's or assigning RR's into the sub-adv=
isor ranges in R2 + adding cross-firm RR's in SZ / NR.&nbsp; Where p<span>a=
rent firm users are provisioned separately at each child firm, this results=
 in redundant user setup, inconsistent entitlements, and manual firm switch=
ing when performing cross=E2=80=91firm operational, supervisory, or adminis=
trative activities in legacy systems.&nbsp; CX does not support cross-firm =
access.</span></p>
    <p><span>As </span>CX&nbsp;<span>becomes the primary platform, the abse=
nce of first=E2=80=91class support for parent firm users risks perpetuating=
 these R2 limitations.&nbsp; Without a standardized way to model parent fir=
m relationships and assign cross=E2=80=91firm access, CX cannot fully suppo=
rt centralized operations for multi=E2=80=91entity firm structures.</span><=
/p>
    <p><strong>Delegate Users</strong></p>
    <p>R2 does not explicitly model delegation (e.g. sub-advisory) relation=
ships as a formal firm=E2=80=91to=E2=80=91firm construct.&nbsp; When a cons=
igning PM firm delegates portfolio balancing and trading responsibilities t=
o a sub=E2=80=91advisory PM firm, access is typically enabled through manua=
l, account=E2=80=91level configurations and firm=E2=80=91specific user setu=
ps.&nbsp; These arrangements are difficult to maintain, and often lack clea=
r alignment to the scope and duration of the underlying sub=E2=80=91advisor=
y agreement.</p>
    <p>In CX, PM sub=E2=80=91advisory users are not yet supported as a dist=
inct access model.&nbsp; Without native support for sub=E2=80=91advisory fi=
rm relationships, CX risks inheriting R2=E2=80=99s fragmented entitlement m=
odel, limiting the platform=E2=80=99s ability to securely and efficiently s=
upport delegated portfolio management and trading activities across firms.<=
/p>
    <h3 id=3D"PRDUnifiedMultiFirmAccess-Cross=E2=80=91JourneyPainPoints&amp=
;RiskImplications"><span>Cross=E2=80=91Journey Pain Points &amp; Risk Impli=
cations</span></h3>
    <div class=3D"table-wrap">
     <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width=
: 96.2815%;">
      <colgroup>
       <col style=3D"width: 11.8611%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 26.2193%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 29.7866%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 32.1934%;">
      </colgroup>
      <tbody>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh"><br></th>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Firm Configuration =E2=86=92</th>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Access Lifecycle Management =E2=86=92</t=
h>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Cross-Firm Operations</th>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Key Frictions</th>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#ffecf8 confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#ffecf8">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li data-uuid=3D"2d81e597-f991-49a1-8a32-f12dcac0afa7"><span>Plat=
form-dependent and inconsistent, resulting in no auditability or enforcemen=
t of relationship</span></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"469fc215-9dbf-4c82-8d6f-bbda04915547"><span>Ever=
y new multi=E2=80=91firm relationship requires bespoke setup and institutio=
nal knowledge</span></li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#ffecf8 confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#ffecf8">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li data-uuid=3D"fc972fb9-f954-430d-98c8-9427074f7369">Access is =
granted via multiple requests, free=E2=80=91text notes, or direct admin int=
ervention: no reliable audit trail tying access change to firm relationship=
 decisions</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"c58061d5-93ec-44c3-a8d9-e1498aa43df5">Human erro=
r in RR code entry or access updates can expose unintended data</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"e5e00d12-2111-44a7-94bb-232db9bfb2da">Attestatio=
n reports are incomplete or misleading due to fragmented identities</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"d8d9ccf1-8bd2-498b-ba85-25e112bdfe39">Inability =
to detect over=E2=80=91provisioned or orphaned access</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"5f6863b6-a2d5-45ca-ba32-6fc52d5f98b0">Missed dea=
ctivation of one or more accounts leads to lingering access</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#ffecf8 confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#ffecf8">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li data-uuid=3D"8c4cb2e2-000e-4d7a-a9e1-6ab562398ae4">Same indiv=
idual is represented by multiple user accounts across firms or RR codes, OR=
 have cross-firm RR's that cannot be verified against the firm relationship=
</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"20e3bca8-461e-4f74-9037-e6c329cbba97">Basic oper=
ational tasks (e.g. trade, approvals, data exports) are repeated with multi=
ple logins</li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Opportunities</th>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#e3fcef confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#e3fcef">
         <ul title=3D"">
          <li data-uuid=3D"41a453cf-728f-40a5-88d6-3e5a73b90d1d">Formalize =
(store, enforce) the relationship structures in CX</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"f5d1d663-89a3-489f-924b-dc5885d44df4">Onboard no=
n-digital workflows and integrate up/downstream</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#e3fcef confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#e3fcef">
         <ul style=3D"text-align: left;" title=3D"">
          <li data-uuid=3D"ccc34a96-80d3-4a87-85ef-bbd3c1fb6194">
           <p><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">Harmonize cross-firm provision=
ing rules and workflow across platforms</span></p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"dbbb7567-d437-4c9c-ac81-8bc31f1a0c98"><span>Prov=
ide visibility for firm security stewards on which users belong to which fi=
rm relationship - strengthen auditability</span></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"024a5161-9c7e-482c-b9e0-4d0f396f7ec7">Facilitate=
 firm relationship offboarding</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"highlight-#e3fcef confluenceTd" data-highlight-colour=
=3D"#e3fcef">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"5fbbf56f-6c96-4cd2-864e-5def81f327a4"><span styl=
e=3D"color:#172b4d;">Enable single ID to grant access to multiple firms</sp=
an></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"629dae0d-e9f3-4d53-bc38-06afda481a63">Introduce =
appropriate feature &amp; data access aggregation / inheritance&nbsp;depend=
ing on the type of relationship</li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
      </tbody>
     </table>
    </div>
    <p><br></p>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
